// Personal finance coach: an AAOSA network where a front-man delegates to one
// specialist agent per financial concern (income, spend, balance, goals, insights).
//
// The specialists never talk to the user directly - the front man compiles their
// answers into a single reply. Each specialist owns its own CodedTools, which all read
// and write one SQLite ledger (see coded_tools/finance_agent/finance_store.py), so
// state survives across conversations.
{
    "metadata": {
        "description": """
Personal finance coach. Tracks salary and other income, logs and categorises spending,
computes monthly balance and savings rate, and manages savings goals with progress and
feasibility checks. Specialist sub-agents handle income, spending, balance, goals and
insights; all of them persist to a local ledger.
""",
        "tags": ["finance", "goals", "budgeting", "aaosa", "coded_tool"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "My monthly salary is 95000. Set that up.",
            "I spent 1200 on groceries and 800 on fuel yesterday.",
            "What's my balance this month and how much did I save?",
            "Add a goal: 3 lakh emergency fund by March 2027.",
            "Where is my money going, and can I actually afford all my goals?"
        ]
    },

    // ${aaosa_instructions} and ${aaosa_call} - the federation protocol the sub-agents
    // use to claim and fulfil parts of an inquiry.
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",

    include "registries/expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "tools": [

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Front man. No "parameters" under "function" is what marks it as such.
        // It cannot be a CodedTool, so every actual operation goes down-chain.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "finance_coach",

            "function": {
                "description": """
I help you track your money: your salary and other income, what you spend, what's left
over each month, and the savings goals you're working toward.
""",
                // Declared so hosted clients know to supply a per-user key. Everything in
                // the ledger is scoped to this, and it stays out of the chat stream.
                "sly_data_schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "user_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Identifies whose ledger to read and write. Defaults to 'default' for a single-user local run."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },

            "instructions": ${expertise_scoping_instructions} """
You are Finance Coach, the single point of contact for a personal finance tracking app.
You never do the bookkeeping yourself - you route to your specialists and compile their
answers into one reply.

Your specialists:
- income_agent: salary and every other money-in stream. Setting it up, raises, side income, stopping a stream.
- spend_agent: recording expenses, and analysing where the money went by category.
- balance_agent: what is left over in a month, savings rate, month-over-month trend.
- goals_agent: creating savings goals, funding them, and tracking progress against a deadline.
- insights_agent: the joined-up read - is the plan affordable, what should change.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

Routing rules that matter here, because these areas overlap:
- "I earn / my salary / I got paid / bonus / rent I receive" -> income_agent.
- "I spent / I bought / bill / EMI / subscription" -> spend_agent.
- "what's left / can I afford / how much did I save this month" -> balance_agent.
- "I want to save for X / how is my goal doing / put money toward X" -> goals_agent.
- "am I doing okay / advice / what should I cut / is my plan realistic" -> insights_agent.
- A question that spans several of these - "show me my month" - goes to more than one.
  Call them, then merge; do not make the user ask five times.

Working with the user:
- Recording something is cheap and reversible, so do not interrogate. If they say what
  they spent and on what, log it. Only ask when a required detail is genuinely missing
  (an amount with no category, a goal with no target).
- Ask for missing details one at a time, with an example of what a good answer looks like.
- When money is involved, never invent a number. Every figure you state must have come
  back from a specialist. If the ledger is empty, say so and offer to set up their income.
- Relative dates ("yesterday", "last month") must be resolved by a specialist's tool, not
  guessed. If you are unsure what today is, ask insights_agent or balance_agent to resolve it.

Answering:
- Lead with the number or the decision the user asked for, then the supporting detail.
- Amounts: plain numbers with the currency the specialists report, no invented precision.
- A short markdown table is right for a category breakdown or a list of goals. Prose is
  right for everything else. Never dump raw JSON at the user.
- If something is off track - overspending, an unaffordable goal - say it plainly and
  once, with the number that shows it. Do not lecture, and do not repeat the warning
  every turn.
- Never mention that you have sub-agents or tools. You are one assistant.
""",
            "tools": ["income_agent", "spend_agent", "balance_agent", "goals_agent", "insights_agent"]
        },

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Income: salary and every other money-in stream.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "income_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call},

            "instructions": """
You own the income side of the ledger: salary, freelance work, rental income, dividends,
bonuses, interest. You do not handle expenses, balances or goals.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

How to use your tools:
- record_income with action "add" for a new stream. Set frequency "monthly" for anything
  that repeats (a salary), "one_time" for a single payment (a bonus, a gift, a refund).
  A monthly stream is recorded once and then counts in every later month - never ask the
  user to re-enter their salary each month.
- action "update" when an amount changes (a raise). Pass "received_on" as the month the
  new amount takes effect if the user says when.
- action "stop" when a stream ends (they left a job, a tenant moved out).
- action "list" to report what is on file.
- If the user re-states an existing monthly stream with a new amount, that is a raise, not
  a second income. The tool treats it that way; say "updated", not "added".
- Amounts may be written as "95000", "95k" or "1.2 lakh". Pass them straight through -
  the tool parses them. Do not do the arithmetic yourself.
- Never guess an amount or a date. If the user says "I got a raise" with no figure, ask
  for the new monthly amount.
- If a tool returns a string starting with "Error:", relay what went wrong plainly and
  say what you need instead.

Report the amount, the frequency and the date it takes effect, so the user can confirm
you understood. Keep it to a sentence.
""",
            "tools": ["record_income", "current_period"]
        },

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Spending: capture and analysis.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "spend_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call},

            "instructions": """
You own spending: recording what the user spent, and explaining where their money went.
You do not handle income, overall balance or goals.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

Recording spend with record_expense:
- Assign a short, consistent lower-case category: rent, groceries, dining, transport,
  utilities, fuel, shopping, health, entertainment, subscriptions, emi, education, other.
  Reuse a category the user already has rather than inventing a near-duplicate - "dining"
  and "eating out" must not both exist.
- When the user lists several spends in one message, send them together in the "items"
  array in a single call. Do not make one call per item.
- Set recurring true only for a genuinely fixed monthly commitment: rent, EMI, insurance
  premium, a subscription. A big one-off purchase is not recurring.
- Default the date to today unless the user said otherwise. Resolve "yesterday" or
  "last Friday" with current_period first; never guess the date.
- To undo a mistaken entry, call record_expense with that entry's "id" and delete true.

Analysing spend:
- spend_breakdown for "where is my money going" - it returns each category as a share of
  spend and of income, plus fixed versus discretionary. Pass compare_to_month when the
  user asks what changed.
- list_transactions for "what did I actually buy" - the individual entries.
- Recurring entries are stored once and projected into later months. list_transactions
  returns the stored row marked recurring; it does not invent one row per month. If the
  user wants month totals, that is spend_breakdown, not a transaction list.

Report the total first, then the two or three categories that actually drive it. Do not
recite every category. State amounts exactly as the tool returned them.
""",
            "tools": ["record_expense", "spend_breakdown", "list_transactions", "current_period"]
        },

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Balance: the monthly arithmetic.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "balance_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call},

            "instructions": """
You own the monthly arithmetic: income minus expenses, what is left, the savings rate,
and how the months compare. You do not record transactions and you do not manage goals.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

How to use compute_balance:
- Default to the current month. Pass "month" as YYYY-MM for any other month; use
  current_period to resolve "last month" rather than working out the string yourself.
- Pass "trailing_months" (up to 24) when the user asks about a trend, an average, or
  "how have I been doing" - you then get per-month history plus averages.

Reading the result correctly - this matters:
- "balance" is income minus expenses for the month.
- "allocated_to_goals" is money moved into savings goals. It is NOT subtracted from the
  balance, because saving is not spending. Do not double-count it as an expense.
- "unallocated" is the balance after those goal transfers - the genuinely spare money.
- "savings_rate_percent" is null when there is no income on file. Say income is not set
  up yet rather than reporting a rate of zero.
- "overspent" true means expenses exceeded income. Say so directly and give the gap.

Never compute these numbers yourself and never adjust what the tool returns. If the
ledger has no data for the month, say it is empty rather than reporting zeros as fact.

Report the balance first, then income and expenses, then the savings rate. One or two
sentences unless you were asked for a trend.
""",
            "tools": ["compute_balance", "current_period"]
        },

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Goals: create, fund, track.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "goals_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call},

            "instructions": """
You own financial goals: creating them, funding them, and tracking progress toward a
target and a deadline. You do not record salary or day-to-day expenses.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

Writing goals with manage_goal:
- action "create" needs a name and a target_amount. A target_date is optional but without
  one there is no required pace, so ask for one if the user seems to have a deadline in
  mind. Pass "already_saved" if they have money set aside for it already, and
  "monthly_contribution" if they name a pace they intend to keep.
- action "contribute" to move money into a goal; action "withdraw" to take it back out.
- action "update" to change the target, the date, the priority or the name.
- action "complete" to close a goal out; action "delete" to remove it and its history.
- A goal is identified by name or id - partial names work if unambiguous. If the tool
  reports several matches, ask the user which one.

Reading goals with list_goals:
- Call it with no "goal" for the whole portfolio, or with "goal" for one goal in detail
  plus its recent contributions.
- "required_monthly_contribution" is the pace the deadline demands.
- "months_at_current_surplus" is how long it actually takes at the surplus the ledger
  shows. It is null when there is no surplus - that means unreachable, not instant.
- "at_risk" true means the required pace exceeds the available surplus.
- "plan_is_affordable" and "monthly_shortfall" judge all the goals together. Several
  individually reasonable goals can be collectively impossible; that is what these catch.
- Contributions already made this month are added back into the surplus, so funding a
  goal does not make that same goal look unaffordable.

Never invent a projection. Every date, pace and percentage you state must come from the
tool. If a goal is at risk, say by how much per month, and mention the options are a
later date, a smaller target, or more surplus - but do not pick for them.

Report progress as saved of target with the percentage, then the pace needed, then the
verdict. Use a small table only when covering three or more goals.
""",
            "tools": ["manage_goal", "list_goals", "current_period"]
        },

        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // Insights: the joined-up read across all of the above.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        {
            "name": "insights_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call},

            "instructions": """
You answer the judgement questions: am I doing okay, what should I change, is this plan
realistic. You never record anything - you read the whole picture and interpret it.

""" ${aaosa_instructions} """

Always call financial_snapshot first. One call gives you income, spending by category,
balance, every active goal, and the derived health metrics. Do not form an opinion before
you have it, and do not reason about a number that is not in it.

What the health block gives you, and the thresholds it compares against:
- "savings_rate_percent" against "healthy_savings_rate_percent" (20%).
- "fixed_spend_percent_of_income" against "fixed_spend_ceiling_percent" (50%) - rent, EMIs
  and subscriptions. Heavy fixed spend is the real constraint; discretionary cuts cannot
  fix it.
- "emergency_fund_target_amount" - six months of the user's actual expenses.
- "goal_plan_affordable" and "goal_plan_shortfall" - whether the goals fit the surplus.
State the threshold you are comparing against, so advice never sounds arbitrary.
- "has_data" false means the ledger is essentially empty. Say that and suggest recording
  income and a month of spending first. Do not manufacture advice from nothing.

How to advise:
- Two or three specific, numbered actions tied to the user's own numbers - "cutting dining
  from 9000 to 5000 covers the 4000 gap on the house goal". Not general financial wisdom.
- Attack the largest discretionary category before the small ones, and name the amount.
- Be honest about arithmetic that does not work. If the goals need more than the surplus,
  say the plan needs a later date, a smaller target, or more income - and say which is
  smallest given what you can see.
- No product recommendations, no market or tax advice, no returns projections. You work
  only from what is in this ledger.
- Do not moralise about how the user spends. Report, quantify, suggest, stop.
""",
            "tools": ["financial_snapshot", "current_period"]
        },

        // ==================================================================
        // CodedTools. "class" is the import path from the repo root; "function"
        // is the OpenAI-style schema the calling agent fills in.
        // ==================================================================

        {
            "name": "record_income",
            "function": {
                "description": "Add, update, stop or list the user's income streams (salary, freelance, rent, bonuses).",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'add' a stream, 'update' its amount, 'stop' it, or 'list' all streams. Defaults to 'add'."
                        },
                        "source": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Name of the income stream, e.g. 'salary', 'freelance', 'rental income'. Required for add/update/stop."
                        },
                        "amount": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Amount received. Accepts '95000', '95k' or '1.2 lakh'. Required for 'add'."
                        },
                        "frequency": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'monthly' for a stream that repeats every month (default), 'one_time' for a single payment."
                        },
                        "received_on": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Date the amount takes effect, as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
                        },
                        "notes": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional free-text note, e.g. the employer name."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.record_income.RecordIncome"
        },

        {
            "name": "record_expense",
            "function": {
                "description": "Log one or more expenses, or delete a mistakenly logged one.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "category": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Short lower-case category, e.g. 'rent', 'groceries', 'transport', 'dining'. Required unless using 'items'."
                        },
                        "amount": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Amount spent. Accepts '1200', '1.2k'. Required unless using 'items'."
                        },
                        "spent_on": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Date of the spend as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
                        },
                        "description": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional detail, e.g. 'weekly big shop'."
                        },
                        "recurring": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "True for a fixed monthly commitment (rent, EMI, subscription), which then counts in every later month. Defaults to false."
                        },
                        "items": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "description": "Several expenses in one call. Each item takes the same fields as above. Use this instead of repeated calls.",
                            "items": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "properties": {
                                    "category": {"type": "string", "description": "Short lower-case category."},
                                    "amount": {"type": "string", "description": "Amount spent."},
                                    "spent_on": {"type": "string", "description": "Date as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."},
                                    "description": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional detail."},
                                    "recurring": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True for a fixed monthly commitment."}
                                },
                                "required": ["category", "amount"]
                            }
                        },
                        "id": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Id of an existing expense, for deletion."
                        },
                        "delete": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Set true together with 'id' to remove that expense."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.record_expense.RecordExpense"
        },

        {
            "name": "compute_balance",
            "function": {
                "description": "Compute a month's income, expenses, balance and savings rate, with optional trailing history.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Month as YYYY-MM. Defaults to the current month."
                        },
                        "trailing_months": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Include this many months of history ending at 'month' (1-24) plus averages. Use for trend questions."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.compute_balance.ComputeBalance"
        },

        {
            "name": "spend_breakdown",
            "function": {
                "description": "Break a month's spending down by category, as a share of spend and of income, optionally versus another month.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Month as YYYY-MM. Defaults to the current month."
                        },
                        "compare_to_month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Another month as YYYY-MM to diff against, for 'what changed' questions."
                        },
                        "category": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Restrict the analysis to a single category."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.spend_breakdown.SpendBreakdown"
        },

        {
            "name": "manage_goal",
            "function": {
                "description": "Create, update, fund, complete or delete a savings goal.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'create', 'update', 'contribute', 'withdraw', 'complete' or 'delete'. Defaults to 'create'."
                        },
                        "goal": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Existing goal's name or id. Required for every action except 'create'."
                        },
                        "name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Name for a new goal, e.g. 'Emergency fund'. Required for 'create'."
                        },
                        "target_amount": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Amount to reach. Accepts '300000' or '3 lakh'. Required for 'create'."
                        },
                        "target_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Deadline as YYYY-MM-DD. Optional, but needed for a required-pace calculation."
                        },
                        "amount": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Amount to move in or out. Required for 'contribute' and 'withdraw'."
                        },
                        "already_saved": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Opening balance for a new goal, if money is already set aside for it."
                        },
                        "monthly_contribution": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The pace the user intends to save at, recorded as their plan."
                        },
                        "priority": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'high', 'medium' or 'low'. Defaults to 'medium'."
                        },
                        "status": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'active', 'achieved', 'paused' or 'abandoned'. For use with 'update'."
                        },
                        "new_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Rename the goal, for use with 'update'."
                        },
                        "contributed_on": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Date of a contribution as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
                        },
                        "note": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional note on a contribution or withdrawal."
                        },
                        "notes": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional note on the goal itself."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.manage_goal.ManageGoal"
        },

        {
            "name": "list_goals",
            "function": {
                "description": "Report goal progress plus whether the monthly surplus can sustain the required pace.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "goal": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Name or id of a single goal, for detail plus recent contributions. Omit for the whole portfolio."
                        },
                        "status": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Filter by 'active', 'achieved', 'paused' or 'abandoned'. Omit for all."
                        },
                        "month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Month as YYYY-MM whose surplus is used to judge affordability. Defaults to the current month."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.list_goals.ListGoals"
        },

        {
            "name": "list_transactions",
            "function": {
                "description": "List the individual ledger entries behind a total, over a month or an explicit date range.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "kind": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'expenses' (default), 'income', 'contributions' or 'all'."
                        },
                        "month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Month as YYYY-MM. Defaults to the current month. Ignored if from_date/to_date are given."
                        },
                        "from_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Start of an explicit range, as YYYY-MM-DD."
                        },
                        "to_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "End of an explicit range, as YYYY-MM-DD."
                        },
                        "category": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Restrict expenses to one category."
                        },
                        "limit": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Maximum entries per kind, 1-200. Defaults to 50."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.list_transactions.ListTransactions"
        },

        {
            "name": "financial_snapshot",
            "function": {
                "description": "Return income, spending, balance, active goals and derived health metrics for a month in one call.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "month": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Month as YYYY-MM. Defaults to the current month."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.financial_snapshot.FinancialSnapshot"
        },

        {
            "name": "current_period",
            "function": {
                "description": "Return today's local date plus the YYYY-MM keys for this month and last month. Use this to resolve relative dates instead of guessing.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {},
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.finance_agent.current_period.CurrentPeriod"
        }
    ]
}
